        <div style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 10px;">Two rivers. One strip of land between them. Two countries that each said it was theirs.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65;">In 1845, Texas joined the United States, and a problem came along with it. No one agreed on where Texas ended in the southwest. You will see how that argument turned into a war, and how Texans took part in it.</div>
    </div>
    <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #D0D9E8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="font-size: 11px; color: #c7922c; margin-bottom: 14px;">&#127919; BY THE END OF THIS LESSON YOU WILL BE ABLE TO&hellip;</div>
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <div style="min-width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; background: #C7922C; color: #fff; font-size: 13px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;">1</div>
            <div style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65;"><strong>I will be able to</strong> explain why the land between the <a href="#foreign" style="border-bottom: 1.5px dotted #C7922C; cursor: help; color: #0E1C42; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" title="NWAY-ses. Spanish for &quot;nuts.&quot; The name of the Nut River."><em>Nueces</em></a> and the <a href="#foreign" style="border-bottom: 1.5px dotted #C7922C; cursor: help; color: #0E1C42; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" title="REE-oh GRAN-day. Spanish for &quot;Big River.&quot;"><em>Río Grande</em></a> was <a href="#glossary" style="border-bottom: 1.5px dotted #C7922C; cursor: help; color: #0E1C42; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" title="Argued over. Each side says it is right.">disputed</a>.</div>
