    <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border-top: 3px solid #C7922C; border: 1px solid #D0D9E8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="font-size: 11px; color: #c7922c; margin-bottom: 14px;">&#128218; PART 3 &middot; THE RANGERS GO TO WAR</div>
<h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;">Texans in the Army</h3><p style="font-size: 17px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Texans did not wait on the sidelines. Many Texas <a href="#glossary" style="border-bottom: 1.5px dotted #C7922C; cursor: help; color: #0E1C42; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" title="A person who joins an army by choice, usually for a short time, instead of being a full-time soldier.">volunteer</a>s joined Taylor&rsquo;s army. Among them were Texas Rangers, men who had spent years fighting on the frontier. Two of the best known were Jack Hays and Samuel Walker. Hays led a regiment of Texas horsemen. Walker had been a prisoner in Mexico before the war, and he knew the country.</p><p style="font-size: 17px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">The Rangers were used for what they did best. They rode fast and shot well from horseback. They worked as <a href="#glossary" style="border-bottom: 1.5px dotted #C7922C; cursor: help; color: #0E1C42; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;" title="A soldier who rides ahead of an army to look over the land and find the enemy.">scout</a>s, carried messages, and struck quickly. In September 1846, Rangers fought in the streets of Monterrey, a city in northern Mexico. Walker also worked with the inventor Samuel Colt to design a larger, stronger revolver, which was later called the Walker Colt.</p><h3 style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;">Two Facts to Hold Together</h3><p style="font-size: 17px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Both Hays and Walker had shown courage in many fights before 1846, not in just one. That steady kind of courage is why officers trusted them with dangerous work.</p><p style="font-size: 17px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">But the Rangers were feared in Mexico for another reason too. Many Mexican civilians remembered them for cruelty. An honest account has to hold both facts.</p><p style="font-size: 17px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Texans had joined the United States to be safer. Now the first thing their new country did was go to war over the border Texas claimed. That was one of the costs of belonging.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border-top: 3px solid #C7922C; border: 1px solid #D0D9E8; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="font-size: 11px; color: #c7922c; margin-bottom: 12px;">&#128170; WHAT TO CARRY FORWARD</div>
        <p style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A border is only a line until someone decides to defend it. Texas claimed the R&iacute;o Grande. Mexico claimed the Nueces. Polk chose to send an army into the space between. As you read about the war, ask who chose what, and what each person might have done differently.</p>
